                <pb facs="0738" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg648"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thayer to Mr.
                            Wilkins</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Albany</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 30,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Have British or Canadian boats, loading at any Canadian port or in ballast, ever
                    been prohibited by you from passing Whitehall through the Champlain Canal to the
                    Hudson River?</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>FRANCIS S. THAYER, <hi rendition="#italic">Auditor.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Collector Canal-Tolls</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Whitehall.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
